<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia June car registrations up 13.6 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia June car registrations up 13.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian new motor vehicle registrations rose a seasonally adjusted 13.6 percent in June to 62,892, the Australian Bureau of Statistics reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Economists had expected a rise of around 8.0 percent for June.  </p>
<p>				  June 97     May 97    June 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    62,892     55,368     60,398</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 67,666     58,621     63,693</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  59,248     58,615     53,829</p>
<p>The bureau said passenger vehicle registrations rose 14.3 percent in June, adjusted, while other vehicles rose 9.6 percent.</p>
<p>In trend terms, the number of motor vehicle registrations has now risen for nine consecutive months.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
